  triage:title "AICH-S4-FIX-1 batch breaks AI.12 single-host-routing-decision invariant" ;
  triage:description "rust-qa-agent bisected: test canonical_write_router_has_one_host_routing_decision (crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs:160) passes at af2fbb83 (the commit immediately preceding the AICH-S4-FIX-1 batch) but fails at HEAD (7bb63e01), asserting 'AI.12 requires PostWriteRouter::dispatch to make the sole host decision' (left==right check, 0 vs 1). The reconcile_after_success removal done to fix AI22-BLOCK-004 appears to have split or relocated the host-routing decision point. Confirmed via direct bisection against the pre-batch commit, not a stale/flaky test. Reported by quality-mgr in QA verdict for AICH-S4-FIX-1 (feature/pAI-s24-host-qualified-ack-receipt @ 7bb63e01), file /Users/randlee/.config/atm/share/atm-dev/ai24-fix-batch-verdict.md." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:category "architecture" ;
  triage:severity "Blocking" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-25T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:reassignReason "Fixed on the same branch (s24) by commit 6d8ee8c3 ('fix: align AI24 boundary guards with canonical routing'), confirmed by direct diff inspection -- reconcile_after_success renamed/split to reconcile_peer restoring the single host-routing-decision invariant. This matches qa-evidence-master's AICH-S4-FIX2 result (blockers=0, result_time_utc 2026-07-25T08:22:21Z, just after the fix commit). TTL was never updated to closed after the fix landed; no re-fix needed." ;
